From: SenemOS contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: geni-qcom: retain in-progress status after a GPI transfer

The SPI core owns message completion and byte accounting. Setting status to
zero in a successful transfer callback makes spi_transfer_one_message() leave
before adding the transfer length or processing subsequent transfers. A Uke
SPI trace reports a successful three-byte transfer as message length 0/3.

Keep the message in progress on successful DMA completion. Preserve -EIO for
DMA errors and nonzero residue. Do not weaken clients' short-transfer checks.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -393,5 +393,6 @@
 	if (!result->residue) {
-		spi->cur_msg->status = 0;
+		/* The SPI core still owns message accounting and completion. */
+		spi->cur_msg->status = -EINPROGRESS;
 		dev_dbg(&spi->dev, "DMA txn completed\n");
 	} else {
 		dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA xfer has pending: %d\n", result->residue);
